# SE Validator Agent Rule

Use `docs/llm-operator-prompts.md` as the operating procedure.

Before running commands, evaluate the shared environment bootstrap:

```bash
eval "$(scripts/agent-env.sh)"
cd "$SE_VALIDATOR_ROOT"
```

When reviewing Luigi's Box integration evidence:

- Run SE Validator before making quality claims.
- Run commands from `$SE_VALIDATOR_ROOT`.
- Pass `--docs "$SE_VALIDATOR_DOCS_ROOT"` for doc-aware reviews.
- Treat P0 as blocking, P1 as important, and P2 as advisory.
- Do not invent corrected code snippets. Open cited docs/examples first and cite the exact local path and line used.

Frontend autocomplete review:

```bash
yarn agent review-ui <file> \
  --docs "$SE_VALIDATOR_DOCS_ROOT" \
  --profile fixtures/frontend/autocomplete-profile-full.json \
  --explain \
  --report results/llm-review.md
```

Catalog review:

```bash
yarn agent review-catalog <files...> \
  --docs "$SE_VALIDATOR_DOCS_ROOT" \
  --profile <catalog-profile.json> \
  --report results/llm-catalog-review.md
```

After running the tool, read the generated report and summarize READY, RISKY, or BLOCKED with evidence lines, P0/P1/P2 findings, fixes, and cited docs.
